  "type": "task",
  "title": "Move the test runner from Python 3.11 to 3.13 and drop 3.11 from the CI matrix",
  "description": "## Description\n\nThe test runner moves from Python 3.11 to Python 3.13, and Python 3.11 is dropped from the CI test matrix. This is maintenance only: no customer-visible behaviour changes. The repo is the `shop` package (pyproject.toml lines 1-2); its tests live in `tests/test_health.py` and are configured by `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` with `pythonpath = [\"src\"]` (pyproject.toml lines 4-5). The checkout has no `.github/` directory and no CI config, so the location of the CI matrix is not known from the repo (see Notes).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `python3.13 -m pytest` run from the repo root passes (the suite in `tests/`).\n- [ ] No CI matrix, runner image or tox/nox-style config, wherever it lives, lists Python 3.11; Python 3.13 is listed as the test version.\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"3\\.11\"` over tracked files (excluding `.acs` and `.git`) returns no reference to Python 3.11 as a supported or tested version.\n\n## References\n\n<!-- acs:references -->\n<!-- /acs:references -->\n\n## Notes\n\n- PRD trace: none. Technical maintenance, no PRD feature or requirement (no PRD exists in the repo).\n- Gotcha: no CI configuration exists in this checkout (no `.github/`; grep for `3.11`, `3.13`, `python-version` finds nothing outside `.acs`). The CI system and the file holding the matrix must be located by the implementer; if the matrix lives outside this repo, that change is a dependency of this task.\n\nacs-ticket: EVAL-1\n",
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "`python3.13 -m pytest` run from the repo root passes (the suite in `tests/`).",
